     6	## 2026-07-20
     7	
     8	### 1402 — HEV descriptor leak checks now isolate harness-owned resources (BUG-260720-2p4fln rework)
     9	- FIX: The fault and 100-cycle real-HEV regressions no longer use `openDescriptorCount() == baseline` as a pass/fail condition. Each harness instead records its own boundary stop, live SOCKS channels, packet-flow reads/queues, bridge endpoint-close lifecycle stages, and cleanup-close errors; the process-global descriptor baseline/observed delta is retained only in failure diagnostics.
    10	- VERIFICATION: The pinned HEV suite passed 13/13 normally and under ThreadSanitizer. Across 30 full-package `swift test` runs the HEV suite passed 30/30; runs 13 and 28 failed only at the excluded pre-existing `PacketFlowBridgeFaultTests.swift:426` drop-summary flake tracked by BUG-260720-24f9w6. Strict Swift format, boundary/native-dependency checks, `swift build`, and `git diff --check` passed.
    11	
    12	### 1351 — Pre-existing drop-summary flake makes full-package runs ~11% unreliable (review BUG-260720-2p4fln)
    13	- FINDING: `PacketFlowBridgeFaultTests.swift:426` ("drop summaries are window-limited and flush unsummarized drops at stop") intermittently observes 0 `packet_bridge.drop_summary` log messages where 1 is expected. Reviewer measured 6 failures in ~50 full `swift test` runs on the BUG-2p4fln tree and 4/30 on clean base `0d6836d` — pre-existing, not introduced by BUG-2p4fln.
    14	- ROOT CAUSE: Likely explains the unresolved 1256 anomaly (105-test era, same symptom class); that entry's "monitoring" status is now answered: the flake is real, frequent, and in the fault-injection suite delivered by TASK-260715-3dn813.
    15	- STATUS: Out of BUG-2p4fln scope (bridge counters/tests explicitly excluded). Needs its own bug: `make validate-core` currently fails ~1 in 8 runs for unrelated work. Evidence logs: `.temp/BUG-260720-2p4fln/review/full-run-*.log`.
    16	
    17	### 1349 — HEV 100-cycle descriptor-baseline check races cross-suite parallelism (review BUG-260720-2p4fln)
    18	- REGRESSION: New `HEVBridgeIntegrationTests.swift:275` final check `eventually(openDescriptorCount() == baseline)` failed 2 times in ~93 full-package runs (first reviewer `make validate-core` run included); 0 failures in 45+ filtered `--filter HEVIntegrationTests` runs across implementer and reviewer.
    19	- ROOT CAUSE: `openDescriptorCount()` counts process-global descriptors, but Swift Testing runs suites in parallel; flake log `.temp/BUG-260720-2p4fln/review/hev-flake-85.log` shows the fuzz suite still live when the 100-cycle test captured its baseline. Any concurrent suite's descriptor delta between baseline capture and final check breaks exact equality permanently; the 5s poll then times out. `.serialized` only guards within the HEV suite. Same fragile pattern at `HEVBridgeIntegrationTests.swift:230` (fault test, 3s).
    20	- DECISION: Review verdict — product changes accepted on evidence (stats snapshot, single boundary stop, quit-safety, TSan, lint, boundaries all green); task routed to-dev only to make the two descriptor-baseline assertions isolation-safe under full-package parallel runs and re-demonstrate repeatability.
    21	
    22	### 1339 — HEV statistics and teardown lifecycle repaired without changing upstream (BUG-260720-2p4fln)
    23	- FIX: `HEVDescriptorBorrowHandle` snapshots all four HEV traffic counters immediately before an intentional quit and publishes that snapshot after join, before releasing the process lease. The spontaneous-return guard remains intact: Swift never calls upstream quit after main has returned, and endpoint B remains borrower-owned until the bridge closes it after join.
    24	- ROOT CAUSE / DECISION: `boundary.stop()` was a product double invocation (`requestStop()` plus `waitForReturn()`), not a bad integration expectation. A lock-coalesced stop task now invokes the boundary once and lets both lifecycle paths await the same operation; unit and real-HEV cycle tests assert one start/one stop.
